{"kind":"propose","text":"H2 verified-source witness has a concrete prerequisite. `packages/bytes/src/sequence.ts:54–66` requires `isEntry()` before checking the hash and checked genesis association. The byte validator in `packages/bytes/src/records.ts` currently refuses all six sequenced input tags and the new entry fields. Thus the two H2 witnesses that name an actual prepare or relate-producing commit cannot reach the source judgment even with authentic hashes. I propose bringing only bounded canonical prepare/commit entry admission forward into H2, with the same shared parser and keeper. It would leave other unserved tags, the Scope pin guard and H4 runtime untouched. Please rule on this scope and the canonical placement of `position` and `reads`: H1 put them on SequenceEntry and also in the prepare input, but entryOf currently writes only the wrapped Input and omits the top-level fields. Copying checks or bypassing isEntryOf for the tests would not establish the requested verified-source behavior."}